# rtun_watchdog.sh config — deploy to /etc/meshforge/rtun_watchdog.conf
#
# Operator values only; never commit a filled-in copy (MF014).
#
# RTUN_REMOTE: user@host of the endpoint the reverse tunnel dials home to.
# This must be the SAME target the rtun init script uses — if the two drift,
# the watchdog probes one path while rtun maintains another and its verdict
# is meaningless.
#
# Prefer a fleet name over a literal IP where the router can resolve one: a
# hardcoded address on an unreserved-DHCP segment blinds the watchdog the
# moment the endpoint moves. Where the router has no fleet-name resolution,
# an IP is the honest choice — pair it with a DHCP reservation.
RTUN_REMOTE="user@endpoint.example"
